          "id": "b8",
          "kind": "exposition",
          "markdown": "### Code\n\nThe destructor releases the resource when the object leaves scope, even if an exception unwinds the stack.\n\n```cpp\nclass file {\n  std::FILE* f_;\npublic:\n  explicit file(const char* path)\n    : f_(std::fopen(path, \"r\")) {}\n  ~file() { if (f_) std::fclose(f_); }\n};\n\n// a is valid but unspecified after the move\nstd::string a = \"hello\";\nstd::string b = std::move(a);\n```"
        },
        {
          "id": "b9",
          "kind": "callout",
          "variant": "tip",
          "title": "Chair's Tip",
          "markdown": "Keep your eye on the timebox, not the clock. Name the time remaining, protect the queue, and gently close off repetition so the room can decide."
        },
        {
          "id": "b10",
          "kind": "callout",
          "variant": "key_idea",
          "markdown": "*Arrive with a question, not a verdict.*"
        },
        {
